// Start/end illustrations for library exercises, from two free sources:
//   'ek'  Everkinetic line drawings (everkinetic.com), CC BY-SA 4.0: attribution is required wherever they show.
//   'fdb' free-exercise-db photos (github.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db), public domain (Unlicense); used only where
//         Everkinetic has no drawing of the same movement. Credited anyway, by source.
// The WebP files live in public/ex-img/ (Vite copies them next to index.html), loaded lazily by relative
// path so they work on GitHub Pages and from file://. Mapping is generated by scripts/ex-img/map_exercises.py
// (review table: scripts/ex-img/mapping.csv). <key>-a.webp is always the START position and -b the END (EK keys ending
// in 's' are eccentric-first lifts whose drawings were swapped). Unmapped exercises simply get no image.
import { h } from './view.js';

// >>> ex-img map
// @generated by scripts/ex-img/map_exercises.py: our exercise id -> [source, image key]
// source 'ek' = Everkinetic (CC BY-SA 4.0), 'fdb' = free-exercise-db (public domain)
